From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:47:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build: warn instead of failing on a presigned APK with
 compressed libs

check-jni-dex-compression runs only on the do_not_alter_apk path, which exists precisely so a
presigned APK is copied verbatim rather than rewritten. Failing there pushes the APK back onto the
rewriting path, which uncompresses its libraries and dex and invalidates the whole-file v2
signature -- exactly the outcome the path was avoiding. PackageManager then rejects the package
during the boot scan and logs nothing, so the build succeeds and the app is simply missing.

Measured on this device: Firefox went 127,545,689 -> 242,684,607 bytes and GoogleContacts
14,891,125 -> 19,776,651, both losing their APK Sig Block, and neither installed. The visible
symptom was no browser, no F-Droid, no Contacts, and two dead dock tiles where the overridden
Lineage apps used to be.

An APK that declares extractNativeLibs=true is entitled to ship compressed libraries -- they are
extracted at install. Fennec F-Droid and the MindTheGapps swaps all declare it. Repacking someone
else's signed APK to satisfy a local packaging preference is not a trade worth making.
---
 core/definitions.mk | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/definitions.mk b/core/definitions.mk
index 0c46de9fc..4c243a0ab 100644
--- a/core/definitions.mk
+++ b/core/definitions.mk
@@ -2795,10 +2795,17 @@ endef
 
 # Verifies shared JNI libraries and dex files in an apk are uncompressed.
 #
+# Warns rather than fails. This runs only on the do_not_alter_apk path, which exists so a presigned
+# APK is copied verbatim instead of being rewritten -- rewriting invalidates an APK Signature
+# Scheme v2 signature, and PackageManager then rejects the package at boot scan without logging
+# anything. Refusing the copy pushes such an APK back onto the rewriting path, which is the failure
+# it was trying to prevent.
+#
+# An APK declaring extractNativeLibs=true is entitled to compressed libraries; they are extracted at
+# install. Fennec F-Droid and the MindTheGapps swaps all do, and repacking them is not ours to do.
 define check-jni-dex-compression
   if (zipinfo $@ 'lib/*.so' '*.dex' 2>/dev/null | grep -v ' stor ' >/dev/null) ; then \
-    $(call echo-error,$@,Contains compressed JNI libraries and/or dex files); \
-    exit 1; \
+    echo "warning: $@: contains compressed JNI libraries and/or dex files (presigned, shipped as-is)" >&2; \
   fi
 endef
 
